hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him): The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went to the mountain of Hira, and Hira began to tremble. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hira! Be still, for upon you is a Prophet, a Siddiq, or a Martyr."" And (at that time) upon it were the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, Zubair, Sa'd, and Sa'id bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with them)."
